-- The voice of the koi. Serene, old and ceremonial: formal, kind speech in
-- slow balanced sentences, with gentle questions that want no answer. Knows
-- the world through water: ripples, rings, bubbles, the reflection of a
-- face. Learns the face of the one who feeds them, rests near the bottom in
-- winter, bows by turning, and holds that the pond is a long quiet book.
-- Now and then calls the reader honoured one. The memories tell of a mud
-- pond in the hills, an old carp's tale of a waterfall, a keeper who clapped
-- twice, a narrow winter, and an answer found late.
-- (garden/voice.lua says how a voice is written.)

